# My Website — Part 2: Designing the Visuals

## Project Overview
A responsive website built with HTML and CSS, demonstrating:
- External stylesheet with base styles and CSS reset
- Typographic system using a scale and relative units (`rem`)
- Layout with Flexbox (header) and CSS Grid (card grid)
- Responsive design using media queries and breakpoints
- Interactive states (hover, focus) for better UX

## Breakpoints
| Breakpoint | Target device |
|------------|---------------|
| < 480px    | Small mobile  |
| 480–600px  | Mobile        |
| 601–900px  | Tablet        |
| 901px+     | Desktop       |

## Responsive Images
Images use `srcset` and `sizes` attributes to serve different resolutions
depending on the viewport width, improving load times on mobile.

## Changelog
### [Version 2.0] — Part 2 submission
- Added external `style.css` with CSS reset
- Established colour scheme using CSS custom properties (variables)
- Applied typography scale using `rem` units
- Implemented Flexbox layout for header and CSS Grid for project cards
- Added media queries for mobile, tablet, and desktop
- Added responsive images using `srcset` and `sizes`
- Added hover and focus states for interactive feedback
- Improved accessibility (semantic HTML, focus outlines)

